   "args": {
    "summary": "Root cause of the L2-1 failure: an instance error. The girder node had count_per_span = 4, contradicting the description's \"3 per span\". MR-02 computes girder.A = A_single × n_girders and girder.I = I_single × n_girders for precast girders, so with n_girders = 4 the re-check gave A = 4.556 m² / I = 1.420 m⁴, inconsistent with the accepted girder.A = 3.4168 m² and girder.I = 1.0648 m⁴ (which had been derived with 3 girders). Corrected the instance to count_per_span = 3; the MR-02, MR-07 (w, m) and JTG 3362-8.7 (Kv, Kh) formulas then re-execute exactly to the accepted values, and generate_model passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nModel: single simply supported 30 m span, spine-beam 2D idealization, 3 precast prestressed C40 small-box girders combined into one equivalent beam (A = 3.417 m², I = 1.065 m⁴, Ec = 32500 MPa, w = 88.84 kN/m, m = 9.056 t/m). Both abutments on plain laminated elastomeric bearings (2 per girder end = 6 per line, 300×400 mm, 5 layers × 8 mm, te = 0.04 m, S = 10.71): Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m, vertical/longitudinal springs, rotation free. Highway Class II, two-way, 2 lanes (qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN, ξ = 1.0), impact factor μ = 0.2006 from f1 = 3.402 Hz.\n\nResults: vertical frequencies 3.402 / 13.485 / 29.876 Hz; self-weight support reactions 1332.55 kN each; self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kNm; lane-load max positive moment 6449.6 kNm."
   },
